  "text": "None of the three solutions can be verified, and each one's key step is unsupported.\n\n- **Solution 1 (q−1):** It asserts an F_q-linear relation at weight q involving ζ(q) and ζ(q−1,1) without an explicit identity. The Carlitz-Bernoulli fact that ζ(q−1) lies in K·π̃^{q−1} gives a relation over K(T), not one with constant F_q coefficients, so it does not establish a failure at weight q.\n- **Solution 2 (q+2):** Distinct leading valuations up to weight q+2 would show independence in that range, but the claimed coincidence at weight q+3 only permits a relation. Its assertion that \"such a relation exists (as is known)\" is unsupported. The valuation formula is also asserted without derivation.\n- **Solution 3 (q):** The q=2 check is a dimension count over K = F_q(T), not over F_q, so it does not show an F_q-linear relation at weight 3. The recurrence d(w) = d(w−1) + d(w−q) is attributed to Todd without a source, and the claimed Frobenius-type mechanism is not spelled out.\n\nI cannot confirm the threshold from memory, and I have no search results in this session to check against. So I cannot identify a correct expression for w_max, and none of the three proposed values can be confirmed.\n\nCHOICE: NONE",
